WHAT YOU'LL LEARN IN THIS LESSON
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

This lesson focuses on building the GroceryList component using fake/mock
data and displaying grocery items dynamically.

You will understand:

• Creating fake/mock grocery data

• Designing a consistent item structure

• Initializing state with sample data

• Rendering arrays using map()

• Using stable keys

• Displaying item details

• Filtering items

• Marking items as purchased

• Deleting items

• Showing an empty state

• Calculating statistics

• Deriving values from state

• Styling a list-based UI

• Preparing the component for a future data source


WHY THIS LESSON IS IMPORTANT
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Fake data is useful during frontend development because it lets you build
and test the UI before a real backend is connected.

The central pattern is:

FAKE DATA
    ↓
STATE
    ↓
FILTER
    ↓
map()
    ↓
LIST ITEMS
    ↓
USER ACTION
    ↓
STATE UPDATE
    ↓
UI UPDATE


This teaches several fundamental React skills:

• Array rendering

• Conditional rendering

• Immutable updates

• Derived data

• Event handling

• State-driven styling


