PART 2: UNDERSTANDING FAKE DATA
================================================================================

WHAT IS FAKE DATA?
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Fake data is sample information created for:

• Development

• Prototyping

• UI design

• Component testing

• Demonstrations

• Learning


Other common names:

• Mock Data

• Sample Data

• Seed Data

• Fixture Data


================================================================================
WHY USE FAKE DATA?
================================================================================

Fake data allows you to:

• Develop the UI without waiting for a backend

• See how realistic information fits the layout

• Test empty and populated states

• Test different categories/statuses

• Reproduce the same UI state

• Debug predictable scenarios

• Design the expected data contract


================================================================================
GOOD FAKE DATA CHARACTERISTICS
================================================================================

Good fake data should:

• Match the planned production-data structure

• Include realistic field types

• Include multiple values/categories

• Include both boolean states where relevant

• Have unique IDs

• Be easy to understand

• Include useful edge cases when testing


