================================================================================
WHY KEEP FAKE DATA OUTSIDE THE COMPONENT?
================================================================================

Instead of putting a large data array directly inside:

GroceryList()


you can use:

import {
  FAKE_GROCERIES
} from '../data/fakeGroceries'


Benefits:

• Component is easier to read

• Sample data is reusable

• Test fixtures can be maintained separately

• UI logic and data definitions remain separated


================================================================================
DATES IN FAKE DATA
================================================================================

Storing:

createdAt:
'2026-10-01T10:30:00Z'


as a string is convenient because it resembles JSON/API data.

If a Date object is needed:

const createdDate =
  new Date(
    item.createdAt
  )


IMPORTANT:
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

JSON does not preserve JavaScript Date objects.

After serialization/deserialization, a timestamp is normally represented
as a string unless you explicitly convert it.


