================================================================================
PART 6: DISPLAYING THE LIST
================================================================================

THE LIST RENDERING PROCESS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

1. Start with groceryItems

2. Apply current filter

3. Produce filteredItems

4. Check if filteredItems is empty

5. If empty:
   show empty state

6. Otherwise:
   call map()

7. map() creates one card per item

8. key identifies each rendered item

9. Item properties become JSX

10. React renders the resulting elements


================================================================================
FILTER
================================================================================

const filteredItems =
  groceryItems.filter(
    item => {

      if (
        filter ===
        'PURCHASED'
      ) {

        return item.purchased
      }


      if (
        filter ===
        'UNPURCHASED'
      ) {

        return !item.purchased
      }


      return true
    }
  )


================================================================================
MAP
================================================================================

{filteredItems.map(
  item => (

    <article
      key={item.id}
    >

      {item.name}

    </article>

  )
)}


================================================================================
WHY key={item.id}?
================================================================================

React uses keys to associate rendered list entries with item identity across
renders.

Prefer:

key={item.id}


instead of:

key={index}


when the data has stable IDs and items can be:

• Deleted

• Reordered

• Inserted

• Updated


================================================================================
CONDITIONAL CLASS
================================================================================

className={
  `item-card ${
    item.purchased
      ? 'purchased'
      : ''
  }`
}


If:

item.purchased = false


Class becomes:

item-card


If:

item.purchased = true


Class becomes:

item-card purchased


================================================================================
EMPTY STATE
================================================================================

There are two different empty conditions.


CASE 1: NO SOURCE ITEMS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

groceryItems.length === 0


Message:

No items in your grocery list.


CASE 2: ITEMS EXIST, BUT FILTER RETURNS NONE
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

groceryItems.length > 0

AND

filteredItems.length === 0


Message:

No items match this filter.


These represent different user situations and should ideally have different
messages.


