PART 7: HANDLING LIST INTERACTIONS
================================================================================

TOGGLE PURCHASED
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

const handleTogglePurchased = (
  id
) => {

  setGroceryItems(
    previousItems =>

      previousItems.map(
        item =>

          item.id === id
            ? {
                ...item,

                purchased:
                  !item.purchased
              }
            : item
      )
  )
}


FLOW:
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Item ID
   ↓
map()
   ↓
Is This the Matching Item?
   │
   ├── NO
   │    ↓
   │   Return Existing Item
   │
   └── YES
        ↓
       Copy Item
        ↓
       Toggle purchased
        ↓
       Return New Item
   ↓
New Array
   ↓
setGroceryItems()


================================================================================
IMMUTABILITY
================================================================================

DON'T:
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

item.purchased =
  !item.purchased


DON'T:
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

groceryItems.push(
  newItem
)


Instead create:

• New array

• New object for changed item


Example:

{
  ...item,

  purchased:
    !item.purchased
}


