DELETE ITEM
================================================================================

const handleDeleteItem = (
  id
) => {

  setGroceryItems(
    previousItems =>

      previousItems.filter(
        item =>
          item.id !== id
      )
  )
}


Before:

[
  Milk,
  Bread,
  Apples
]


Delete:

Bread


After:

[
  Milk,
  Apples
]


================================================================================
WHY FUNCTIONAL STATE UPDATES?
================================================================================

The new items array depends on the previous items array.

Therefore prefer:

setGroceryItems(
  previousItems => ...
)


This avoids depending on a particular rendered snapshot of:

groceryItems


================================================================================
FILTER CHANGE
================================================================================

Filter buttons only change:

filter


Example:

setFilter(
  'PURCHASED'
)


Then:

filteredItems

is derived again from:

groceryItems + filter


